# Local, UNTRACKED ssh host entries. Copy to ~/.ssh/config.local and edit.
#
# This file is pulled in by the committed ~/.ssh/config via `Include`. Put every
# real host here: personal, work, and anything you do not want in git.
#
# Globals (AddKeysToAgent, IdentitiesOnly, ForwardX11 no, ...) come from the
# committed config. A host inherits them unless it sets its own value.
#
# Enable X11 forwarding only on the hosts that need it. Prefer ForwardX11 over
# ForwardX11Trusted. Never set `StrictHostKeyChecking no` except as a last
# resort on a throwaway box.

# Example: public git remote.
# Host github.com
#   User         git
#   IdentityFile ~/.ssh/your_ed25519

# Example: host reached through a bastion/tunnel, with its own key.
# Host internal-box
#   HostName     10.0.0.10
#   User         ubuntu
#   IdentityFile ~/.ssh/some_key
#   ProxyCommand ssh bastion -W %h:%p

# Example: a host that genuinely needs X11.
# Host gui-box
#   HostName   10.0.0.11
#   ForwardX11 yes
